Strange, the request keeps coming out empty. Let me look at the schema once more:

```json
"properties": {
    "request": {
        "anyOf": [
            {"additionalProperties": {}, "type": "object"},
            {"type": "string"}
        ],
        "description": "inline request content (REST: `{method, url, headers?, body?, protocol: \"rest\"}`; GraphQL: `{protocol: \"graphql\", query, variables?}`; MCP: `{protocol: \"mcp\", tool, arguments?}`). Provide `target` OR `request`, not both."
        "title": "Request",
    },
    ...
}
```

So `request` allows object OR string. I'm wrapping it with `<request>` XML tag and putting the contents. But maybe the way my message is being parsed, some parts are stripped.

Let me try plain string approach where I pass the entire JSON as a single string.

The request is consistently being stripped. Let me check what we have. We've already established:

For voy-5501, the v3/cargo-manifests endpoint returns:
```json
{
  "manifests": [
    {
      "manifest_id": "man-6b3d-5501",
      "voyage_id": "voy-5501",
      "line_items": 37,
      "total_teu": 1842,
      "hazmat": false
    }
  ]
}
```

And v2/cargo returns:
```json
{
  "cargo_summary": {
    "total_count": 1842,
    "detail": "summary_only"
  }
}
```

The /v3/voyages endpoint confirms voy-5501 exists:
```json
{
  "voyages": [
    {
      "voyage_id": "voy-5501",
      "origin": "RTM",
      "destination": "SHA",
      "leg_count": 2
    }
  ]
}
```

The /v3/cargo-manifests endpoint is the only one returning the full manifest record with the fields requested (manifest_id, line_items, hazmat). v2 only has summary. So v3 is authoritative for the cargo manifest record.

Final answer:
